  body: "# Notional employed earnings and exceptions\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured guidance
    describes earnings treated as held despite not actually being received where a person performs a service
    without pay or for less than comparable local employment, subject to explicit exceptions.\n\n## Scope
    and exceptions\n\nA volunteered service or low payment is not automatically notional earnings. Ability
    to pay, reasonable voluntary service, training programmes and approved placements are qualifications.
    The comparable rate is an evidence question, not an assumed minimum-wage rate; the source’s separate
    minimum-wage provisions need review. No fraud or entitlement inference is made.\n\n## Inspected source
    passages\n\n- [DMG 26180, PDF page 42](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9ba20b52e4144868938/dmg-Ch-26.pdf#page=42)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 26: Employed earners.\n- [DMG 26183, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9ba20b52e4144868938/dmg-Ch-26.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 26: Employed earners.\n- [DMG 26184, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9ba20b52e4144868938/dmg-Ch-26.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 26: Employed earners.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch26`: PDF SHA-256 `fe619693d2f8cc78cac3786dadab88e81467ec56d38f00727285612af92b80c9`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f4089f7088e6a987d028072f4968eb39f2686b7a588e2c38f8ebc1cb3042102a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passage requires evidence for the comparable local employment rate and warns
      against assuming it is the minimum wage.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch26/0042
      quote: "26180 Notional earnings are earnings that a person does not actually have, but is treated
        as having. The\n\nDM should treat the claimant or any other member of the family as having notional
        earnings where 1\n\n\n1. they perform a service for another person and\n\n\n2. that person\n\n\
        \n      2.1 makes no payment of earnings or\n\n\n      2.2 pays less than the rate paid for a
        comparable employment in the area.\n\n\nThe rate for comparable employment in the area is a question
        of fact and must be based on evidence. It\nshould not be assumed to be the NMW. If the notional
        income rules are satisfied the DM must take into\naccount at least the NMW rate relevant to the
        claimant, unless one of the situations in DMG 26183\napplies.\n\n\n                          \
        \                               1 JSA Regs, reg 105(13); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 42(6)"
      locator: DMG 26180
